How to Run AI Interview Coach (Beginner Guide)
What You Need Installed

Before running the project, install:

1. Python 3.11

Check:

python --version

Should show something like:

Python 3.11.x
2. Node.js

Check:

node -v
npm -v

If both show version numbers, you're good.

Project Structure

The project folder should look like:

AI Interview Coach
│
├── backend
└── frontend
Step 1: Start the Backend

Open Command Prompt.

Go to backend:

cd "X:\AI Interview Coach\backend"

Activate virtual environment:

.venv\Scripts\activate

You should see:

(.venv)

at the start of the line.

Now start the backend:

python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload

If successful, you'll see:

Uvicorn running on http://127.0.0.1:8000

Leave this window open.

Step 2: Start the Frontend

Open a second Command Prompt.

Go to frontend:

cd "X:\AI Interview Coach\frontend"

Install packages (first time only):

npm install

Start frontend:

npm run dev

You'll see something like:

Local: http://localhost:5173

Leave this window open too.

Step 3: Open the Website

Open your browser.

Go to:

http://localhost:5173

The AI Interview Coach website should open.

If Registration/Login Doesn't Work

Check that:

Backend is running

Open:

http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

If a page opens, backend is working.

MongoDB is configured

Backend needs a valid MongoDB connection string in:

backend/.env

Without it, registration and login will fail.

If You Get Missing Package Errors

Backend:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Frontend:

npm install
Every Time You Want To Run The Project

Open 2 terminals.

Terminal 1
cd "X:\AI Interview Coach\backend"
.venv\Scripts\activate
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload
Terminal 2
cd "X:\AI Interview Coach\frontend"
npm run dev

Then open:

http://localhost:5173

That's it. The project should now be running locally on your computer.
